 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Line 73 has no attribute. `eval_algebraMap` (line ~189) is `@[simp]` and rewrites to `MvPolynomial.eval\u2082 (Int.castRingHom R) (fun p => M p.1 p.2) P`. No simp lemma has the leading-minor product as its argument; `eval_leadingBlockMinorProduct` is unannotated and needs an explicit `rw`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/LDU/Coordinates.lean",
   "fix": "Tag `leadingBlockMinorProduct_mvPolynomialX_eval\u2082` with `@[simp]` and leave `eval_leadingBlockMinorProduct` untagged, since simp would then prove it. Its left side is a substitution applied to a constant that is not unfolded, so it does not overlap with Mathlib's simp lemmas.",
   "issue": "`leadingBlockMinorProduct_mvPolynomialX_eval\u2082` is the normal-form lemma for substituting a matrix into the generic leading-minor product, but it is not `@[simp]`. After the simp lemma `eval_algebraMap` fires on `F.eval (algebraMap _ _ (leadingBlockMinorProduct b (mvPolynomialX m m \u2124)))`, simp is stuck on `MvPolynomial.eval\u2082 \u2026 (leadingBlockMinorProduct b (mvPolynomialX m m \u2124))`. This is the shape consumers of `exists_polynomial_coordinate` meet.",
   "line": 73
  }
 ],
